§§ `First sentence: who is not covered`

-- Not a Freeman: the sentence speaks of a Freeman and of no one else.
#ASSERT `chapter 29, first sentence: what is done to a Freeman` FALSE `taken` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered by chapter 29`
#ASSERT `chapter 29, first sentence: what is done to a Freeman` FALSE `condemned` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered by chapter 29`
#ASSERT `chapter 29, first sentence: what is done to a Freeman` FALSE `exiled` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered by chapter 29`
#ASSERT `chapter 29, first sentence: what is done to a Freeman` FALSE `taken` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not covered by chapter 29`
-- A treatment the sentence does not list: the sentence says nothing of it.
#ASSERT `chapter 29, first sentence: what is done to a Freeman` TRUE `some other treatment` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered by chapter 29`
#ASSERT `chapter 29, first sentence: what is done to a Freeman` TRUE `some other treatment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not covered by chapter 29`

§§ `First sentence: who the text names as doing it`

-- Only "nor will We ... pass upon him, nor condemn him" names an actor: We.
#ASSERT `chapter 29, first sentence: the party the text names as doing it` `passed upon` EQUALS JUST `the King`
#ASSERT `chapter 29, first sentence: the party the text names as doing it` `condemned` EQUALS JUST `the King`
-- The passive limbs, and "some other treatment", name no one: NOTHING, not a guess.
#ASSERT `chapter 29, first sentence: the party the text names as doing it` `taken` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `chapter 29, first sentence: the party the text names as doing it` `imprisoned` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `chapter 29, first sentence: the party the text names as doing it` `disseised of his Freehold` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `chapter 29, first sentence: the party the text names as doing it` `disseised of his Liberties` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `chapter 29, first sentence: the party the text names as doing it` `disseised of his free Customs` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `chapter 29, first sentence: the party the text names as doing it` `outlawed` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `chapter 29, first sentence: the party the text names as doing it` `exiled` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `chapter 29, first sentence: the party the text names as doing it` `any other wise destroyed` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `chapter 29, first sentence: the party the text names as doing it` `some other treatment` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Last sentence: Justice or Right, to any man`

-- Arguments: the person is a man, the thing dealt in.
#ASSERT `chapter 29, last sentence: selling, denying or deferring` TRUE Justice EQUALS `forbidden by chapter 29`
#ASSERT `chapter 29, last sentence: selling, denying or deferring` TRUE Right EQUALS `forbidden by chapter 29`
-- Neither Justice nor Right: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT `chapter 29, last sentence: selling, denying or deferring` TRUE `another thing` EQUALS `not covered by chapter 29`
-- Not a man in the text's sense: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT `chapter 29, last sentence: selling, denying or deferring` FALSE Justice EQUALS `not covered by chapter 29`
#ASSERT `chapter 29, last sentence: selling, denying or deferring` FALSE Right EQUALS `not covered by chapter 29`

§§ `Traces of the regulative rules (read back by check-traces.py; build 98 cannot assert a DEONTIC)`

-- First sentence, the King passes upon a Freeman by lawful judgment of his Peers only: not a breach; the prohibition stands.
-- expect: STANDING
#TRACE `chapter 29, first sentence: the King shall not pass upon or condemn a Freeman` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `pass upon a Freeman` TRUE FALSE AT 3
-- ... by the Law of the Land only: not a breach.
-- expect: STANDING
#TRACE `chapter 29, first sentence: the King shall not pass upon or condemn a Freeman` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `pass upon a Freeman` FALSE TRUE AT 3
-- ... by neither: a breach.
-- expect: BREACHED
#TRACE `chapter 29, first sentence: the King shall not pass upon or condemn a Freeman` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `pass upon a Freeman` FALSE FALSE AT 3
-- Condemning, by neither: a breach.
-- expect: BREACHED
#TRACE `chapter 29, first sentence: the King shall not pass upon or condemn a Freeman` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `condemn a Freeman` FALSE FALSE AT 3
-- Condemning, by both: not a breach.
-- expect: STANDING
#TRACE `chapter 29, first sentence: the King shall not pass upon or condemn a Freeman` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `condemn a Freeman` TRUE TRUE AT 3
-- Time passing with nothing done: no deadline is stated, so the prohibition stands for ever.
-- expect: STANDING
#TRACE `chapter 29, first sentence: the King shall not pass upon or condemn a Freeman` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100000)

-- Last sentence, the King sells Justice: a breach.
-- expect: BREACHED
#TRACE `chapter 29, last sentence: the King shall not sell, deny or defer Justice or Right` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `deal in Justice or Right` sell Justice AT 3
-- ... denies Right: a breach.
-- expect: BREACHED
#TRACE `chapter 29, last sentence: the King shall not sell, deny or defer Justice or Right` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `deal in Justice or Right` deny Right AT 3
-- ... defers Justice: a breach.
-- expect: BREACHED
#TRACE `chapter 29, last sentence: the King shall not sell, deny or defer Justice or Right` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `deal in Justice or Right` defer Justice AT 3
-- ... sells something that is neither Justice nor Right: the sentence is silent, so no breach.
-- expect: STANDING
#TRACE `chapter 29, last sentence: the King shall not sell, deny or defer Justice or Right` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `deal in Justice or Right` sell `another thing` AT 3
-- Time passing with nothing done: the prohibition stands.
-- expect: STANDING
#TRACE `chapter 29, last sentence: the King shall not sell, deny or defer Justice or Right` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100000)
